The Last Lighthouse Keeper: credits for third-party material

Picture
- Drawn entirely in code (three.js paper layers). Engine files src/lib.js, src/paper.js, src/stage.js, src/post.js
  are adapted from the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), MIT licence.
- three.js (threejs.org), MIT licence.
- Font: IM FELL English by Igino Marini (www.iginomarini.com), SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  Reserved Font Name "IM FELL English Roman" (subset shipped in the library's core/fonts/).

Voice
- Narration synthesised with Kokoro-82M (github.com/hexgrad/kokoro, Apache License 2.0) through kokoro-onnx
  (github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx, MIT), voice "bm_george".

Music and sound
- Original score, written for this film. Harp, kalimba and music box are physically modelled in code
  (Lemo-Opuscar core/audio/pluck.py, MIT); celesta, string pad and ship horn are synthesised in numpy.
- All foley (sea, wind, footsteps, door, flare, clockwork, chimes) is procedurally synthesised
  (Lemo-Opuscar core/audio/sfx.py, MIT). No samples or recordings from third parties.

Story, script, characters and design: original. The lighthouse, the keeper "Elias" and the ship are fictional.
